{%- comment -%}
  LOCAL OVERRIDE. Changed from the gem: every card links to its detail page,
  through the title stretched over the card so the icon links are not nested
  inside it; the thumbnail is `project-thumb.liquid` (a gradient when there is
  no image); and the github icon became every link as an icon row
  (`project-links.liquid`).

  Every project has a detail page. Whether that page carries the white sheet is
  decided by `_layouts/project.liquid` from the body being empty or not, so
  nothing here has to be flagged per project.
{%- endcomment -%}
<div class="col">
  <div class="card h-100 project-card hoverable">
    {% include project-thumb.liquid project=project class='project-thumb--card' %}
    <div class="card-body">
      {%- comment -%}
        Year from `period` ("2025.05 - 2025.07"), else from `date`. A project
        that ran across a new year shows both.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- if project.period -%}
        {%- assign y_start = project.period | slice: 0, 4 -%}
        {%- assign y_end = project.period | split: '-' | last | strip | slice: 0, 4 -%}
      {%- else -%}
        {%- assign y_start = project.date | date: '%Y' -%}
        {%- assign y_end = y_start -%}
      {%- endif -%}
      <h3 class="card-title">
        <a class="project-card__main" href="{% if project.redirect %}{{ project.redirect }}{% else %}{{ project.url | relative_url }}{% endif %}">
          {{- project.title -}}
        </a>
      </h3>
      {%- if project.subtitle %}
        <p class="project-card__subtitle">{{ project.subtitle }}</p>
      {%- endif %}
      {%- comment -%}
        No `description` here. It repeated what `subtitle` says in the same size
        and color, and three lines of it per card pushed the grid to one row per
        screen. The card is a pointer; the description opens the detail page as
        its intro, which every project has (`has_detail: true`).
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- comment -%}
        Links and year share one row on the card floor. The year used to be
        positioned out of the flow, which let it sit on top of whatever ended
        up in that corner (a wrapped tech tag, on a project with no links).

        A project with no links would leave that row's left half empty, so the
        tags move down into it and the row above disappears.
      {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- assign has_links = false -%}
      {%- if project.github or project.demo or project.links -%}{%- assign has_links = true -%}{%- endif -%}
      {%- capture tags -%}
        {%- if project.tech_stack -%}
          <ul class="project-card__tags" aria-label="tech stack">
            {%- for tech in project.tech_stack %}
              <li>{{ tech }}</li>
            {%- endfor %}
          </ul>
        {%- endif -%}
      {%- endcapture -%}
      {%- if has_links %}{{ tags }}{% endif %}
      <div class="project-card__footer">
        {%- unless has_links %}{{ tags }}{% endunless %}
        {% include project-links.liquid project=project style='icon' %}
        <p class="project-card__year">
          {{ y_start -}}
          {%- unless y_end == y_start %} - {{ y_end }}{% endunless %}
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</div>
